    "q-10271": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10271",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ such that $\\text{Cov}(x,y)=-6$ and their standard deviations are ${\\sigma }_{x}=2$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}=5.$ Compute the corresponding linear correlation coefficient.",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) linear correlation coefficient for data sets $x$ and $y$ is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting our numbers, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{(-6)}{2\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =-0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
