    "q-134398": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134398",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{23,\\,21,\\,25\\},\\,y=\\{10,\\,8,\\,9\\}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=23,$ $\\overset{―}{y}=9,$ ${\\sigma }_{x}≈1.633,$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}≈0.816.$ Calculate the corresponding linear correlation coefficient. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) linear correlation coefficient of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ is the covariance, and ${\\sigma }_{x}$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}$ are the standard deviations of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the covariance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(23-23)(10-9)+(21-23)(8-9)+(25-23)(9-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(0)(1)+(-2)(-1)+(2)(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ≈0.667\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the formula. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.667}{1.633\\cdot 0.816} \\\\  & ≈0.50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
