    "q-134400": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134400",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{7,\\,2,\\,12\\},\\,y=\\{-1,\\,9,\\,7\\}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=7,$ $\\overset{―}{y}=5,$ ${\\sigma }_{x}≈4.082,$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}≈4.320.$ Calculate the corresponding linear correlation coefficient. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) linear correlation coefficient of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ is the covariance, and ${\\sigma }_{x}$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}$ are the standard deviations of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the covariance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(7-7)(-1-5)+(2-7)(9-5)+(12-7)(7-5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(0)(-6)+(-5)(4)+(5)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[0-20+10] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & ≈-3.333\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the formula. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(-3.333)}{4.082\\cdot 4.320} \\\\  & ≈-0.19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
