    "q-134450": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134450",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The data sets $x$ and $y$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=186,\\,{S}_{xy}=2,\\,{S}_{yy}=96\n$$\n\nCalculate the corresponding linear correlation coefficient. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definitions of ${S}_{xx},$ ${S}_{xy},$ and ${S}_{yy}$ for the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}:$\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\\,{S}_{xy}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\\,{S}_{yy}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\n$$\n\nThe linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ of the data sets $x$ and $y$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}=\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{\\sqrt{{S}_{xx}\\cdot {S}_{yy}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{186}\\cdot \\sqrt{96}} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{2}{13.638\\,182\\cdot 9.797\\,959} \\\\  & ≈0.01\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
