    "q-134454": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134454",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{5,\\,8,\\,2\\},\\,y=\\{-1,\\,2,\\,5\\}\n$$\n\nYou are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=5$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=2.$ Calculate the corresponding linear correlation coefficient.",
      "worked_solution": "The linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}=\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{\\sqrt{{S}_{xx}\\cdot {S}_{yy}}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(5-5)(-1-2)+(8-5)(2-2)+(2-5)(5-2) \\\\  & =(0)(-3)+(3)(0)+(-3)(3) \\\\  & =0+0-9 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we compute the sums in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(5-5)^{2}+(8-5)^{2}+(2-5)^{2} \\\\  & =0+9+9 \\\\  & =18 \\\\ {S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & =(-1-2)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(5-2)^{2} \\\\  & =9+0+9 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{(-9)}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{18}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{-9}{3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
