    "q-134404": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134404",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "An ergonomist investigates $4$ factories. He wants to check the strength of the linear correlation between $x,$ the money spent by factory owners on safety training courses, and $y,$ the number of accidents per year in the factories. The data is shown below.\n\n| **Money spent (hundreds of $$$)** | **$10$** | **$15$** | **$12$** | **$23$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of accidents** | $3$ | $6$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\nYou are given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=15$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\rho ≈-0.45$\n\nII. There is a strong negative correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\nIII. There is a weak negative correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\nHint: $|\\rho |>0.7$ indicates a strong correlation, and $0.3\\le |\\rho |\\le 0.7$ indicates a weak correlation.",
      "worked_solution": "The linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{\\text{Cov}(x,y)}{{\\sigma }_{x}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{y}}=\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{\\sqrt{{S}_{xx}\\cdot {S}_{yy}}}.\n$$\n\nIn addition, we have the following rule of thumb:\n\n- if $|\\rho |>0.7,$ the correlation is *strong*\n\n- if $0.3\\le |\\rho |\\le 0.7,$ the correlation is *weak*\n\n- if $|\\rho |<0.3,$ then the correlation is *negligible*\n\nLet's now examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. To calculate $\\rho ,$ we first compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(10-15)(3-4)+(15-15)(6-4) \\\\  & +(12-15)(5-4)+(23-15)(2-4) \\\\  & =(-5)(-1)+(0)(2)+(-3)(1)+(8)(-2) \\\\  & =5+0-3-16 \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we compute the sums in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(10-15)^{2}+(15-15)^{2}+(12-15)^{2}+(23-15)^{2} \\\\  & =25+0+9+64 \\\\  & =98 \\\\ {S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & =(3-4)^{2}+(6-4)^{2}+(5-4)^{2}+(2-4)^{2} \\\\  & =1+4+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{98}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & ≈-\\frac{14}{9.899\\,495\\cdot 3.162\\,278} \\\\  & ≈-0.45,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. Since $0.3\\le |\\rho |\\le 0.7,$ the correlation is weak. Also, since $\\rho $ is negative, the correlation is negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
